Currently: optional::transform never materializes against gcc-16
headers and main verifies vacuously (0 assertions).  Sibling of
cpp23_optional_monadic (which uses the host's headers).

ROUND-104 TRIAGE: the first error is `symbol '_M_payload' is unknown`
while instantiating _Optional_base<int, TRUE, TRUE>.  gcc-16's payload
is `_Storage<_Stored_type> _M_payload;` where _Storage is a NESTED
member UNION template with a defaulted bool NTTP
(`template<typename _Up, bool = is_trivially_destructible_v<_Up>>`)
and P0848 conditionally-trivial destructors (`~_Storage() = default;`
plus `constexpr ~_Storage() requires (!is_trivially_destructible_v<_Up>)`).
Four hand kernels all PASS (negative results, /tmp/k104/os1-os4):
plain constrained dual dtor; union with defaulted trait NTTP; the same
nested inside a class template; variable-template trait in the NTTP and
requires-clause.  Per the no-hand-guessing rule the carrier is being
cvise-reduced instead: /tmp/cv105, gate = pinned driver + tumbleweed
g++ 16.2 validity (docker image gcc16-gate, via `sg docker` -- root-owned
`sudo` children crash cvise's kill_pid_queue with psutil.AccessDenied)
+ CBMC `_M_payload' is unknown` + `could not fully type-check`.
